From: Flax <hmccanne@exclamationpoint.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Restore Configuration: trigger the factory reset that this
 platform actually has

NetFn 0x30 / cmd 0x02 has always been registered and allowlisted, and it looks
like a working factory reset -- it takes the 'C','L','R' confirmation and the
0xAA/0xBB/0xCC operations, and it answers with a plausible status byte.  It
does nothing.  All it does is write /tmp/.rwfs/.restore_op, and nothing in this
image reads that file: the path belongs to Intel's FWUPD_INTEL_FEATURES rwfs
layout, which is disabled in this build, so on TiogaPass the directory does not
exist and the write simply fails.

The reset this platform does have is the one Redfish drives, via
xyz.openbmc_project.Common.FactoryReset Reset() on the software manager.  On a
static-norootfs machine that sets the U-Boot one-shot key openbmconce to
factory-reset; the initramfs step 21-factory-reset reads the key on the next
boot and 30-ubiattach-or-format then runs ubiformat on the rwfs volume, which
discards the upper layer of the /etc, /var and /home overlays.  Call that
instead of writing the dead file.

Deliberately no reboot.  bmcweb follows its Reset() with a graceful restart, so
the Redfish button reboots the BMC on the operator's behalf; a raw IPMI command
that silently drops the BMC is a worse default, and the reset is armed either
way.  The operator reboots when ready.  This is a deliberate difference in
behaviour between the two paths, not an oversight.

The status subcommand now reads openbmconce back rather than stat-ing the dead
file, because nothing else holds that state -- the key is consumed by the
initramfs and cleared by clear-once.service.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [platform-specific]

---
--- a/src/oemcommands.cpp
+++ b/src/oemcommands.cpp
@@ -3114,6 +3114,55 @@
     return ipmi::responseSuccess();
 }
 
+static constexpr const char* factoryResetService =
+    "xyz.openbmc_project.Software.BMC.Updater";
+static constexpr const char* factoryResetPath = "/xyz/openbmc_project/software";
+static constexpr const char* factoryResetIntf =
+    "xyz.openbmc_project.Common.FactoryReset";
+static constexpr const char* factoryResetEnvName = "openbmconce";
+static constexpr const char* factoryResetEnvValue = "factory-reset";
+
+/*
+ * True when a factory reset is armed but has not happened yet.
+ *
+ * FactoryReset.Reset() arms the reset by setting the U-Boot one-shot key
+ * openbmconce to factory-reset.  The initramfs step 21-factory-reset consumes
+ * that key on the next boot and clear-once.service clears it afterwards, so
+ * reading the key back is the only honest source for "pending" -- there is no
+ * daemon holding that state.
+ */
+static bool factoryResetArmed()
+{
+    try
+    {
+        boost::process::ipstream is;
+        boost::process::child c(fwGetEnvCmd, "-n", factoryResetEnvName,
+                                boost::process::std_out > is);
+
+        bool armed = false;
+        std::string line;
+        while (c.running() && std::getline(is, line))
+        {
+            if (line.find(factoryResetEnvValue) != std::string::npos)
+            {
+                armed = true;
+            }
+        }
+        c.wait();
+
+        // fw_printenv exits non-zero when the key is simply unset, which is
+        // the ordinary "nothing armed" case rather than an error.
+        return c.exit_code() == 0 && armed;
+    }
+    catch (const std::exception& e)
+    {
+        phosphor::logging::log<phosphor::logging::level::ERR>(
+            "ipmiRestoreConfiguration: cannot read U-Boot environment",
+            phosphor::logging::entry("ERROR=%s", e.what()));
+        return false;
+    }
+}
+
 ipmi::RspType<uint8_t /* restore status */>
     ipmiRestoreConfiguration(const std::array<uint8_t, 3>& clr, uint8_t cmd)
 {
@@ -3128,8 +3177,6 @@
     constexpr uint8_t cmdFullRestore = 0xbb;
     constexpr uint8_t cmdFormat = 0xcc;
 
-    constexpr const char* restoreOpFname = "/tmp/.rwfs/.restore_op";
-
     switch (cmd)
     {
         case cmdStatus:
@@ -3138,14 +3185,30 @@
         case cmdFullRestore:
         case cmdFormat:
         {
-            // write file to rwfs root
-            int value = (cmd - 1) & 0x03; // map aa, bb, cc => 1, 2, 3
-            std::ofstream restoreFile(restoreOpFname);
-            if (!restoreFile)
+            /*
+             * All three operations do the same thing here.  Upstream
+             * distinguishes a default restore, a full restore and a format,
+             * but this platform has exactly one reset -- ubiformat of the rwfs
+             * volume -- so the distinction has nothing to select.  They are all
+             * accepted rather than rejected so that existing tooling built
+             * against the Intel command keeps working.
+             */
+            std::shared_ptr<sdbusplus::asio::connection> busp = getSdBus();
+
+            try
+            {
+                auto method = busp->new_method_call(
+                    factoryResetService, factoryResetPath, factoryResetIntf,
+                    "Reset");
+                busp->call(method);
+            }
+            catch (const std::exception& e)
             {
+                phosphor::logging::log<phosphor::logging::level::ERR>(
+                    "ipmiRestoreConfiguration: FactoryReset failed",
+                    phosphor::logging::entry("ERROR=%s", e.what()));
                 return ipmi::responseUnspecifiedError();
             }
-            restoreFile << value << "\n";
 
             phosphor::logging::log<phosphor::logging::level::WARNING>(
                 "Restore to default will be performed on next BMC boot",
@@ -3160,10 +3223,8 @@
     constexpr uint8_t restorePending = 0;
     constexpr uint8_t restoreComplete = 1;
 
-    uint8_t restoreStatus = std::filesystem::exists(restoreOpFname)
-                                ? restorePending
-                                : restoreComplete;
-    return ipmi::responseSuccess(restoreStatus);
+    return ipmi::responseSuccess(factoryResetArmed() ? restorePending
+                                                     : restoreComplete);
 }
 
 ipmi::RspType<uint8_t> ipmiOEMGetNmiSource(void)
